"""Installment 10, wave 07: George Lamming's 1946-2000 bibliography (Caribbean writing in English).

The first Caribbean author of installment 10. All six novels (1953-1972) and the three
books of essays (1960, 1992, 1995) are recorded. They were checked against the Wikipedia
articles on Lamming, In the Castle of My Skin and The Emigrants; Encyclopaedia Britannica;
three Gale reference entries compiled on Encyclopedia.com (Contemporary Black Biography,
Contemporary Novelists with Gerald Moore's essay, and the Encyclopedia of African-American
Culture and History); Gale's Novels for Students on In the Castle of My Skin, whose
chapter-by-chapter summary was read in full; and, through search-result extracts only,
EBSCO Research Starters on Season of Adventure and Natives of My Person, passages from
Helen Tiffin and Avis G. McDonald quoted on eNotes, the Google Books record of
Conversations, an Anthurium article and the University of Michigan Press's description of
Season of Adventure. None of the books was read.

Sources disagree on the date of Natives of My Person (1972, or 1971 in Britannica), on the
century of its setting (sixteenth or seventeenth), on the first US edition of The Emigrants
(1954 or 1955), on the US edition of Season of Adventure (1998 or 1999) and on the titles
and dates of Coming, Coming Home. Each record states the disagreement. Every work is linked
to "Caribbean Literature in English"; the three books written about, or set among, West
Indians in England (The Emigrants, The Pleasures of Exile, Water with Berries) are also linked
to "Black British Writing and the Windrush Generation", whose taxonomy entry names The
Emigrants. No other movement is assigned.
"""

import os
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(__file__))
from i10_lib import A10, W10, G, T, M, MAJ  # noqa: E402

